# this container's mounts + service, both lanes
#
# build-spec — comfyui runtime declaration, sourced by the shared resolver
# (droste-entrypoint.sh / distrobox init_hooks -> droste-resolve.sh). Contract +
# ordering: base/resolve/build-spec.example. All paths EXPLICIT and ABSOLUTE;
# $HOME expands at source time (sourced bash).

# ── SERVICE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ComfyUI web UI on 8188 with the upstream Strix Halo perf flags. The extra
# model-paths config lives on /opt/program-cache (seeded if_missing by
# templates.yaml) and registers the baked /opt/resources/model_configs — CACHE
# class per the taxonomy: a re-seeded pointer file, never user work. main.py is
# absolute: ComfyUI derives every path from base_path = main.py's directory, not
# CWD (PRE_LAUNCH still cd's there for any relative writes).
#
# SPLIT IN TWO because the argv now has a USER-CONFIGURABLE MIDDLE: comfyui_argv
# rebuilds SERVICE as HEAD + the flags translated from comfyui.cfg + TAIL. What
# stays in these two arrays is what this file does not translate — the bind
# address, the port, and the model-paths config. The two perf flags that
# used to sit here, --disable-mmap and --disable-smart-memory, became the
# WEIGHT_LOADING and MODEL_RESIDENCY settings and are emitted from the table below
# at their defaults.
# ⚠️ THAT IS NOT THE SAME COMMAND LINE, and it is deliberate: WEIGHT_LOADING's
# default `eager` still emits --disable-mmap, but MODEL_RESIDENCY's default is
# `cache`, whose right-hand side is EMPTY — so --disable-smart-memory is no longer
# on the shipped line. `9f95652 Expose the last two overrides, and change two
# comfyui defaults` is where that happened; comfyui.cfg's `{evict, cache*}` is the
# authority on which default is current, and this comment follows it.
# ⚠️ --extra-model-paths-config is nargs='+', so it STAYS LAST: any later token
# that does not begin with `-` would be swallowed as a second config path.
# ⭐ THE ADDRESS AND THE PORT ARE DROSTE DEFAULTS HERE, NOT CONSTANTS (s60). They used
# to be owned by server.env; they are DROSTE_COMFYUI_HOST and DROSTE_COMFYUI_PORT now,
# in comfyui.cfg, and serve::apply_host / serve::apply_port REWRITE the token after
# --listen and after --port before the service is launched. So what these two literals
# are is the answer a box gets when its user set neither — and the argv a direct
# `podman run` of this image gets, where no launcher runs at all.
# ⚠️ DO NOT TRANSLATE EITHER OF THEM IN comfyui_argv. The launcher reads the same two
# cfg keys through droste::cfg_get and is the only place that validates them (an IPv4
# literal, one message on all five boxes); a second reader here would be a second
# mechanism that agrees with it only until one of the two changes.
# 🚨 THE INTERPRETER IS ABSOLUTE, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING (measured on Loaf, s65).
# A bare `python` here resolved to /usr/bin/python in the `distrobox enter` lane and
# the service died on the first third-party import (`No module named 'sqlalchemy'`)
# while serving fine from the init hook.
# ⚠️ AND THE CAUSE IS NOT THE DOCUMENTED ONE. `ENV PATH=` is not LOST to the login
# shell here — it SURVIVES and is ordered BEHIND it:
#   /srv/.local/bin:…:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:…:/opt/venv/bin:/opt/rocm/bin:…
# so /usr/bin wins and /opt/venv/bin never gets asked. ⭐ That is nastier than the
# vanished-PATH case, because the directory IS on the PATH: any check that asks
# "is /opt/venv/bin present?" passes while `python` still resolves to the wrong one.
# ⭐ WHY THIS BOX ALONE: the other four name PROGRAMS (ds4-server, llama-server,
# vllm) that nothing in /usr/bin shadows. `python` is the one name that COLLIDES
# with a system binary — so they are correct by luck of naming, not by construction.
# ⇒ NEVER put a bare interpreter in an argv that a launcher may build from a login
# shell. Name it absolutely; $VIRTUAL_ENV is /opt/venv, baked in base/Container.runtime.
COMFYUI_ARGV_HEAD=(
    /opt/venv/bin/python /opt/ComfyUI/main.py
    --listen 0.0.0.0 --port 8188
)
COMFYUI_ARGV_TAIL=(
    --extra-model-paths-config /opt/program-cache/extra_model_paths.yaml
)
# A usable argv on its own, and comfyui_argv rebuilds it FROM THE TWO ARRAYS
# rather than appending to it — so calling PRE_LAUNCH twice cannot grow it.
SERVICE=( "${COMFYUI_ARGV_HEAD[@]}" "${COMFYUI_ARGV_TAIL[@]}" )

# ── HEALTH — probe endpoint for droste-healthcheck.sh ────────────────────────
# ComfyUI serves its web UI at / (200) and has no dedicated health route.
HEALTH_PATH="/"
HEALTH_ACCEPT="ok"

# ── CFG_FILE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Seeded from templates/comfyui.cfg (templates.yaml if_missing) and never
# overwritten — the user's edits win. ComfyUI reads NO env var for any of these
# knobs, so comfyui_argv translates the DROSTE_COMFYUI_* values into flags.
# No export loop (unlike ds4/llama): nothing downstream reads them from the
# environment, they only ever become argv.
CFG_FILE="/opt/data/comfyui.cfg"

# ── SERVE — the four rows droste-serve.sh reads out of this spec ─────────────
# The five SERVE settings live in the same CFG_FILE as everything else, under the
# prefix below: DROSTE_COMFYUI_STARTUP_ENABLED / _HOST / _PORT / _TLS_CERT / _TLS_KEY.
# serve::read_config PARSES them with droste::cfg_get and never sources the file — that
# read also runs inside the healthcheck every 30s under --health-on-failure=restart,
# where an abort is a restart loop that ejects every shell in the box.
# 🚨 SERVE_CFG_PREFIX IS REQUIRED, and its absence is not a quiet degradation: a spec
# that names CFG_FILE and no prefix makes read_config refuse to serve and report the
# IMAGE as broken, because otherwise all five settings would read as absent and the box
# would silently stop serving.
# ⭐ THE PREFIX IS THE APPLICATION'S NAME. It coincides with the box name here; it does
# not on finetuning, whose settings are DROSTE_JUPYTER_*.
SERVE_CFG_PREFIX="DROSTE_COMFYUI_"
# The flags this box spells differently from the library's defaults. serve::apply_host
# defaults to --host; this box says --listen, and without the row the launcher would
# APPEND a --host that ComfyUI's argparse has never heard of — the server would reject
# its own argv and the box would restart-loop. --port needs no row (all five agree).
SERVE_HOST_FLAG=--listen
# The port a user gets when they set none — ComfyUI's own, and the value comfyui.cfg
# already shows on its commented DROSTE_COMFYUI_PORT line. 🚨 THE ROW IS WHAT MAKES THAT
# LINE TRUE (§7a, ruled s60): the address has a library-wide default and the port had
# none, so before this row an absent port did not mean "use 8188" — it meant the box
# refused to serve. It must stay equal to the literal after --port in COMFYUI_ARGV_HEAD;
# that copy is what a direct `podman run` gets, where no launcher runs at all.
SERVE_PORT_DEFAULT=8188
# ⚠️ THE TLS PAIR HAS NO LIBRARY DEFAULT, deliberately: there is no majority spelling,
# and a wrong flag is not a wrong value — the server rejects the argv and never starts.
# Read at the pin (comfy/cli_args.py:65-66 at COMFYUI_REF 4da9e2db = v0.33.3), and the
# names comfyui.cfg's Security block already documents.
# ⭐ THE FLAGS ARE DECLARED HERE; WHETHER THEY ARE EMITTED IS THE LAUNCHER'S CALL —
# serve::apply_tls emits them ONLY when the user set both, because a flag we emit
# outranks every other way of turning TLS on and a default would destroy that choice.
SERVE_TLS_CERT_FLAG=--tls-certfile
SERVE_TLS_KEY_FLAG=--tls-keyfile

# ── OVERLAYS — <upper>:<lower> ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Baked lowers are load-bearing (venv, the 3 baked custom nodes); user writes
# land in the uppers. Each upper's ROOT is its class: pip installs (incl. bin/
# entry points) are re-runnable → /opt/program-cache, which the installer may
# empty; the user's own node picks and edits are not → /opt/data. (Each .work
# sibling follows its own upper — kernel: workdir and upperdir share a fs.)
OVERLAYS=(
    "/opt/program-cache/venv:/opt/venv"
    "/opt/data/custom_nodes:/opt/ComfyUI/custom_nodes"
)

# ── SURFACES — <src>:<dest> ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# model-tree = the scanner's symlink tree (+ user drop-ins), surfaced over the
# marker-only baked models/. user/ = ComfyUI state (db/settings/workflows),
# seeded if_empty by templates.yaml after the mount. datasets/ = training data
# for ComfyUI's own fine-tune nodes (0.33+): image / image+text / video sets,
# each a subfolder with a metadata.json or safetensors shards. All three are
# DATA. temp/ is the one SCRATCH surface — preview/intermediate files ComfyUI
# writes and never re-reads across starts — so it comes off /opt/program-cache
# (see PRE_LAUNCH, which makes the mounted dir sticky world-writable for both
# lanes).
#
# ⚠️ datasets/ MUST be surfaced at the baked path, not redirected. ComfyUI's
# save node writes to folder_paths.get_folder_paths("datasets")[0] — index 0,
# not a search — and an extra_model_paths.yaml entry only reaches index 0 when
# it carries `is_default: true` (add_model_folder_path appends otherwise).
# Surfacing keeps the built-in path BOTH first and persistent, so the ordering
# question never arises. Unbound, a user's saved training set would live in the
# container and die on the next recreate.
SURFACES=(
    "/opt/data/model-tree:/opt/ComfyUI/models"
    "/opt/data/user:/opt/ComfyUI/user"
    "/opt/data/datasets:/opt/ComfyUI/datasets"
    "/opt/program-cache/tmp:/opt/ComfyUI/temp"
)

# ── CACHES — <src>:<dest> ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Compute/kernel caches persisted under /opt/program-cache/compute/ with zero env
# vars. THE compute/ PREFIX IS LOAD-BEARING: it is exactly what the resolver
# rewrites to the shared /opt/caches store when that volume is bound, so these
# rows — and only these — are cross-box shareable. MIOpen uses BOTH
# ~/.cache/miopen (binary caches) and ~/.config/miopen (its machine-written
# tuning DB — MIOpen's default userdb path, config-ish location notwithstanding).
CACHES=(
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/miopen:$HOME/.cache/miopen"
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/miopen-db:$HOME/.config/miopen"
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/triton:$HOME/.triton/cache"
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/torch:$HOME/.cache/torch"
)

# ── CRITICAL — <label>:<path> ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hard-error if unbound (ALLOW_EPHEMERAL downgrades to a warning). input/output
# hold real user work; the HF cache is the single shared model store (unbound =>
# silent multi-GB re-downloads).
CRITICAL=(
    "input:/opt/ComfyUI/input"
    "output:/opt/ComfyUI/output"
    "hf-cache:$HOME/.cache/huggingface"
)

# ── OPTIONAL — <label>:<path>:<marker> ───────────────────────────────────────
# Optional local-model collection (scanner source #2). Tell-once: INFO + marker
# (body from templates/mount_shared_models_here) on first unpopulated start.
OPTIONAL=(
    "models:/opt/models:/opt/models/mount_shared_models_here"
)

# ── PRE_LAUNCH ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1) The server lane never sources /etc/profile.d (no login shell), but the torch
#    perf env it provides (TORCH_ROCM_AOTRITON_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL,
#    TORCH_BLAS_PREFER_HIPBLASLT) is needed under the served ComfyUI too. Source
#    the exact script the interactive lane uses so both lanes match.
# 2) Refresh the ComfyUI model symlink tree from the shared HF cache (+ optional
#    /opt/models). Defaults already match: tree /opt/data/model-tree, registry
#    /opt/data/model-registry.yaml, cache ~/.cache/huggingface/hub, /opt/models
#    skipped-if-absent. A scanner failure only leaves the tree stale — log and
#    continue, never block the server (the resolver runs under set -e; the ||
#    branch absorbs the failure).
# 3) Rebuild SERVICE from the DROSTE_COMFYUI_* values now that CFG_FILE has been
#    sourced (step 6 of apply_spec; SERVICE would otherwise be final at
#    spec-source time, before the user's file was read).

# DROSTE_COMFYUI_<SUFFIX> → flag maps. Every flag, its spelling and its argparse
# group are read from comfy/cli_args.py at the pinned COMFYUI_REF (4da9e2db =
# v0.33.3); the value vocabulary and the defaults are the ones documented in
# templates/comfyui.cfg, which is the surface the user edits — the two must be
# changed together.
#
# A THIRD SHAPE, because ComfyUI's knobs are neither ds4's value flags nor its
# booleans: nearly all of them are ENUMERATED CHOICES over an argparse
# MUTUALLY-EXCLUSIVE GROUP, where a second member of the group is a hard parse
# error and where the ordinary answer ("normal", every "auto") is NO FLAG AT
# ALL. One variable per group is what makes an illegal pair unwritable, so the
# table is one record per group:
#
#     "<SUFFIX>|<value>=<flags>|<value>=<flags>|…"
#
# ⭐ THREE PROPERTIES, ALL BY CONSTRUCTION RATHER THAN BY CARE:
#   1. AT MOST ONE flag per group is ever emitted — one record, one match, and
#      no flag appears in two records.
#   2. An EMPTY right-hand side is a first-class answer: the group's absent
#      state, which is what ComfyUI's "normal" vram mode IS (there is no
#      --normalvram) and what every "auto" means.
#   3. The FIRST pair is the DEFAULT. It is used when the variable is unset —
#      the shipped state, since every line in comfyui.cfg is commented out — and
#      when it holds something we do not recognise.
# A right-hand side is word-split, so one value can emit a flag WITH its value
# (--preview-method taesd) or TWO flags: MANAGER=legacy must say --enable-manager
# itself. cli_args.py implies it from --enable-manager-legacy-ui, but that was
# measured NOT to be enough on hardware.
COMFYUI_CHOICE_FLAGS=(
    "VRAM|gpu-only=--gpu-only|highvram=--highvram|normal=|lowvram=--lowvram|novram=--novram|cpu=--cpu"
    "DYNAMIC_VRAM|auto=|on=--enable-dynamic-vram|off=--disable-dynamic-vram"
    "ATTENTION|auto=|ck=--use-ck-attention|pytorch=--use-pytorch-cross-attention|quad=--use-quad-cross-attention|split=--use-split-cross-attention"
    "COMPUTE_PRECISION|auto=|fp16=--force-fp16|fp32=--force-fp32"
    "VAE_PRECISION|bf16=--bf16-vae|auto=|fp16=--fp16-vae|fp32=--fp32-vae"
    "UNET_PRECISION|auto=|bf16=--bf16-unet|fp8_e4m3fn=--fp8_e4m3fn-unet|fp8_e5m2=--fp8_e5m2-unet|fp8_e8m0fnu=--fp8_e8m0fnu-unet|fp16=--fp16-unet|fp32=--fp32-unet|fp64=--fp64-unet"
    "TEXT_ENCODER_PRECISION|auto=|bf16=--bf16-text-enc|fp8_e4m3fn=--fp8_e4m3fn-text-enc|fp8_e5m2=--fp8_e5m2-text-enc|fp16=--fp16-text-enc|fp32=--fp32-text-enc"
    "UPCAST|auto=|on=--force-upcast-attention|off=--dont-upcast-attention"
    "PREVIEW|taesd=--preview-method taesd|auto=--preview-method auto|latent2rgb=--preview-method latent2rgb|none=--preview-method none"
    "WEIGHT_LOADING|eager=--disable-mmap|lazy=--mmap-torch-files"
    "MODEL_RESIDENCY|cache=|evict=--disable-smart-memory"
    "CUSTOM_NODES|yes=|no=--disable-all-custom-nodes"
    "MANAGER|modern=--enable-manager|legacy=--enable-manager --enable-manager-legacy-ui|no_ui=--enable-manager --disable-manager-ui"
    "CUDA_MALLOC|auto=|on=--cuda-malloc|off=--disable-cuda-malloc"
)

# Plain numeric passthroughs (GiB, ds4's <SUFFIX>:<flag> shape). Unset — the
# shipped state — means NO FLAG, which is how ComfyUI's own per-OS default
# (400 MiB reserved on Linux) stays in force.
COMFYUI_NUMBER_FLAGS=(
    "RESERVE_VRAM:--reserve-vram"
)

comfyui_is_num() { [[ ${1:-} =~ ^[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$ ]]; }
comfyui_is_int() { [[ ${1:-} =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; }

# ── A BLANK MEANS "GIVE ME THE DEFAULT" HERE, BY CONSTRUCTION (s58) ──────────
# 🚨 THIS BOX NEEDS NO BLANK-GUARD TABLE, and that is a property of the three shapes
# above rather than luck — which makes it a property that can be LOST, so it is stated
# here and enforced by g1lab/cfguard.sh rather than left to be rediscovered.
#
# Jei's three-category rule for an empty value, which every box is audited against:
#   1. a blank CRASHES the server or makes it unhealthy             ⇒ give the default
#   2. the value is NUMERIC or from a practically FINITE set (a
#      boolean, an enum, a menu) — and it does NOT matter whether
#      the blank crashes; behaving differently is enough            ⇒ give the default
#   3. an unbounded string whose blank is NOT the default and could
#      itself MEAN something useful ("no config file", "no cache
#      directory") — all three conditions required                  ⇒ keep the blank
#
# ⭐ comfyui is 100% DROSTE-OWNED — it exposes no native name at all, so every one of its
# 17 settings passes through this function and there is nowhere else for a bad blank to
# be absorbed. Sixteen are category 2 (fourteen enumerated groups, one GiB number, one
# parameterised cache mode) and EXTRA_ARGS is an unbounded string whose blank is the
# shipped state. All 17 already deliver the default when blank, three different ways:
#   * a choice group seeds `flags` from pairs[0] — the documented default — and only
#     REPLACES it inside `if [ -n "$val" ]`, so "" never reaches the match;
#   * a number flag is skipped by `[ -n "$val" ] || continue`, which is how ComfyUI's
#     own per-OS default (400 MiB reserved on Linux) stays in force;
#   * CACHE reads `${DROSTE_COMFYUI_CACHE:-ram}` — `:-`, not `=`, which is correct HERE
#     precisely because there is no category 3 setting on this box to protect. `none` is
#     a VALUE in that group, not a blank.
# ⚠️ SO A NEW SETTING IS THE HAZARD, not the existing ones. Anything that feeds a PATH, a
# REQUIRED argument, or a value with no sensible zero would be the first row on this box
# where an empty string is not the default — and it would need ds4's DS4_BLANK_IS_DEFAULT
# treatment, not one of the three shapes above.

# comfyui_argv — DROSTE_COMFYUI_* → SERVICE. Its own function so it can be
# driven alone (source the spec, call it, print SERVICE) without the mounts, the
# profile.d source or the model scan.
#
# 🚨 A BAD VALUE IS LOUD BUT NEVER FATAL, and that is a decision, not an
# oversight. PRE_LAUNCH runs inside resolve::apply_spec under `set -e` in BOTH
# lanes: a non-zero return here kills the server entrypoint (container restart
# loop) and fails the distrobox init hook, which distrobox reports as a generic
# error — a typo in a config file would take away the easiest way to fix the
# typo. The third caller, serve::build_service on the healthcheck's relaunch
# path, already downgrades a failing PRE_LAUNCH to a warning and launches "with
# the argv as built", so refusing here would not even be consistent between the
# three doors. So every rejected value is NAMED on stderr together with the
# value used instead (the init hook cats that log to the terminal, the
# entrypoint sends it to the container log) and the box comes up in its
# DOCUMENTED DEFAULT state rather than in a fourth state nobody wrote down.
# What must never happen is a knob that looks authoritative and does nothing.
comfyui_argv() {
    local dyn=() entry suffix rest var val def flags pair ok list
    local pairs=() cache mode arg nums=() n bad=0

    for entry in "${COMFYUI_CHOICE_FLAGS[@]}"; do
        suffix=${entry%%|*}
        rest=${entry#*|}
        IFS='|' read -r -a pairs <<<"$rest"
        def=${pairs[0]%%=*}
        flags=${pairs[0]#*=}
        var="DROSTE_COMFYUI_$suffix"
        val=${!var:-}
        if [ -n "$val" ]; then
            ok=0
            for pair in "${pairs[@]}"; do
                if [ "${pair%%=*}" = "$val" ]; then
                    flags=${pair#*=}
                    ok=1
                    break
                fi
            done
            if [ "$ok" -eq 0 ]; then
                list=""
                for pair in "${pairs[@]}"; do
                    list="$list ${pair%%=*}"
                done
                serve::err "$var='$val' is not a valid value — using the default '$def'. Valid values:$list. Fix it in $CFG_FILE and restart the box."
            fi
        fi
        # Word-split ON PURPOSE: the right-hand side is a literal from the table
        # above and never user input, one value may expand to a flag plus its
        # value or to two flags, and an empty side adds nothing at all.
        # shellcheck disable=SC2206
        dyn+=( $flags )
    done

    for entry in "${COMFYUI_NUMBER_FLAGS[@]}"; do
        var="DROSTE_COMFYUI_${entry%%:*}"
        val=${!var:-}
        [ -n "$val" ] || continue
        if comfyui_is_num "$val"; then
            dyn+=( "${entry#*:}" "$val" )
        else
            serve::err "$var='$val' is not a number of GiB — leaving the flag off, so ComfyUI's own default applies. Fix it in $CFG_FILE and restart the box."
        fi
    done

    # CACHE is the one PARAMETERISED knob — <mode>[:<n>[,<n>]] over that same
    # kind of mutually-exclusive group — so it is parsed rather than tabulated.
    # It still emits exactly one member of cache_group, malformed values
    # included: those fall back to the documented default, none.
    cache=${DROSTE_COMFYUI_CACHE:-ram}
    mode=${cache%%:*}
    arg=""
    [ "$cache" = "$mode" ] || arg=${cache#*:}
    case "$mode:$arg" in
        none:)     dyn+=( --cache-none ) ;;
        classic:)  dyn+=( --cache-classic ) ;;
        high-ram:) dyn+=( --high-ram ) ;;
        ram:)      dyn+=( --cache-ram ) ;;
        ram:*)
            # --cache-ram is nargs='*': one threshold, or two, and cli_args
            # itself errors on a third.
            IFS=',' read -r -a nums <<<"$arg"
            ok=1
            [ "${#nums[@]}" -le 2 ] || ok=0
            for n in "${nums[@]}"; do
                comfyui_is_num "$n" || ok=0
            done
            if [ "$ok" -eq 1 ]; then
                dyn+=( --cache-ram "${nums[@]}" )
            else
                bad=1
            fi
            ;;
        lru:*)
            # N >= 1, because main.py selects LRU on `args.cache_lru > 0`:
            # --cache-lru 0 parses fine and then silently is not LRU at all.
            if comfyui_is_int "$arg" && [ "$arg" -ge 1 ]; then
                dyn+=( --cache-lru "$arg" )
            else
                bad=1
            fi
            ;;
        *) bad=1 ;;
    esac
    if [ "$bad" -eq 1 ]; then
        serve::err "DROSTE_COMFYUI_CACHE='$cache' is not a valid value — using the default 'ram'. Valid values: ram ram:GiB ram:GiB,GiB lru:N classic high-ram none. Fix it in $CFG_FILE and restart the box."
        dyn+=( --cache-ram )
    fi

    # Raw catch-all, appended after every tabulated knob so a user's own option
    # is the later one wherever ComfyUI lets a later option win. It stays INSIDE
    # dyn on purpose: COMFYUI_ARGV_TAIL's --extra-model-paths-config is nargs='+'
    # and must remain the last thing on the line. Quoting inside the value IS
    # honoured since s52 and it is not glob-expanded (see
    # comfyui.cfg), matching DROSTE_LLAMA_EXTRA_ARGS and DROSTE_DS4_EXTRA_ARGS.
    # shellcheck disable=SC2206
    mapfile -d '' -t _extra < <(droste::split_args "${DROSTE_COMFYUI_EXTRA_ARGS:-}")
    dyn+=( ${_extra[@]+"${_extra[@]}"} )

    SERVICE=( "${COMFYUI_ARGV_HEAD[@]}" ${dyn[@]+"${dyn[@]}"} "${COMFYUI_ARGV_TAIL[@]}" )
}

PRE_LAUNCH="comfyui_pre_launch"
comfyui_pre_launch() {
    # shellcheck source=/dev/null
    source /etc/profile.d/01-rocm-envs.sh

    # ── the XDG bases comfyui.cfg never names, whose blank strands the caches ───
    # 🚨 A BLANK XDG_CACHE_HOME MOVES THE HF CACHE OUT FROM BEHIND THE CRITICAL BIND,
    # SILENTLY, AND TAKES THE TORCH CACHE WITH IT. Two readers on this box, both with an
    # ABSENT-ONLY default, so a blank base yields a RELATIVE path from each:
    #   huggingface_hub  os.getenv("HF_HOME", os.path.join(
    #                      os.getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME", "~/.cache"), "huggingface"))
    #                                                        (constants.py, ~:158-166)
    #   torch            os.getenv(ENV_TORCH_HOME, os.path.join(
    #                      os.getenv(ENV_XDG_CACHE_HOME, "~/.cache"), "torch"))
    #                                            (torch/hub.py:139-146, READ AT THE PIN
    #                                             v2.9.1 — base/rocm-version.env)
    # MEASURED at hub 1.29.0 in an isolated interpreter, HOME=/home/boxuser, HF_HOME
    # unset:
    #                     absent                                 ""
    #   HF_HOME           /home/boxuser/.cache/huggingface       huggingface
    #   HF_HUB_CACHE      /home/boxuser/.cache/huggingface/hub   huggingface/hub
    # ⇒ both resolve against the process's CWD — and this function cd's to /opt/ComfyUI
    # at its end, so the write lands in the CONTAINER LAYER — instead of
    # $HOME/.cache/huggingface (the hf-cache CRITICAL row) and $HOME/.cache/torch (a
    # CACHES row). The binds still mount and still pass their own checks, which test the
    # PATH and not where a library later decided to write, so the box starts, serves and
    # reports itself HEALTHY while a multi-GB download dies at the next recreate.
    # ⚠️ THE NODE INSTALLER IS THE LIVE ROUTE, not just a hand-run download:
    # ComfyUI-Manager pulls model and node payloads through huggingface_hub, which is
    # UNPINNED here (Container.comfyui installs `huggingface_hub[hf_transfer]`, and
    # Manager's own dependency on it is unpinned too). The reader was measured identical
    # across 0.35.3 → 1.1.0 and again at 1.29.0 — a property of the library, not of one
    # release, so a bump cannot quietly retire this guard.
    # ⚠️ model_scanner.py is NOT the reason this is here and is NOT affected: its
    # resolve_cache_dir() honours HF_HUB_CACHE and HF_HOME and deliberately does not read
    # XDG_CACHE_HOME (see its docstring), so it would keep reporting the bind while the
    # library wrote elsewhere — which is precisely how this stays invisible.
    # ⚠️ FIRST IN THE FUNCTION, BEFORE THE SCANNER SYNC AND BEFORE THE `cd`, so every
    # child this hook spawns already sees the corrected environment.
    # ⚠️ `${XDG_CACHE_HOME-~/.cache}` IS NOT THE SAME FIX — a shell with an empty base
    # yields `/huggingface` where python yields `huggingface`. A third wrong answer.
    # ⚠️ NOT IN droste::blank_is_unset AND IT MUST NOT BE ADDED TO ONE. That helper is a
    # NAMED LIST of natives a box's config file EXPOSES (droste-common.sh:85-90), and
    # this box exposes NO natives at all — there is no such list here to join, which is
    # exactly why the guard sits beside its consumers. Same placement, same mechanism and
    # the same shape approved for vllm in `e4028f2`; one mechanism, not two.
    # ⭐ THE SHAPE OF THIS HOOK DIFFERS FROM ds4's AND finetuning's — comfyui has no
    # `*_env()` companion, because its entire surface is droste-owned and is translated
    # into an argv by comfyui_argv rather than exported. The guard is unaffected: it acts
    # on the ENVIRONMENT the server inherits, which exists either way.
    # ⭐ AND THIS COVERS ROUTES droste::cfg_apply CANNOT SEE — a create-time `--env`, or
    # an `export XDG_CACHE_HOME=` typed inside `distrobox enter` before a download —
    # because it reads the environment the server is about to get, not the file.
    # ⚠️ SILENT, like every other blank guard: the blank IS the request for the default.
    #
    # 🚨 THE GUARD COVERS THE WHOLE XDG BASE-DIRECTORY FAMILY, NOT ONLY THE NAME WITH A
    # MEASURED CONSUMER — RULED BY JEI: "overruled. All XDG variables should be treated
    # the same; it's too confusing to have varying implementation." That DELIBERATELY
    # OVERRIDES "each entry earns its place by a MEASURED difference" FOR THIS FAMILY,
    # and it is "One Surface, Five Servers" pointed inward: a user must not have to
    # learn which box guards which XDG name. It is the second application of the same
    # instinct — s58 ruled the identical widening for the `loud` treatment.
    # ⭐ THE FAMILY IS THE FREEDESKTOP BASE DIRECTORY SPECIFICATION'S SEVEN VARIABLES,
    # IN SPEC ORDER: the four user directories, the runtime directory, and the two
    # search LISTS. The boundary is a document rather than a judgement, which is what
    # makes "all of them" an answerable claim. XDG_BIN_HOME is NOT in the spec (which
    # defines only the ~/.local/bin convention, with no variable) and is excluded; so
    # are the session names (XDG_SESSION_TYPE, XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP, XDG_SEAT, XDG_VTNR,
    # …), which are not directory settings at all and belong to a display stack this
    # image does not run.
    # ⚠️ SIX OF THE SEVEN HAVE NO MEASURED CONSUMER ON THIS BOX, AND THAT IS THE POINT
    # RATHER THAN A DEFECT — uniformity is the requirement here, coverage-per-name is
    # not. XDG_CONFIG_HOME is the one that used to be argued OUT by name: the
    # ~/.config/miopen CACHES row LOOKS like a consumer and is not (MIOpen expands `~`
    # from $HOME with no XDG rung at all, src/expanduser.cpp, and Triton is the same,
    # knobs.py). That reading was correct and is no longer the question being asked.
    # ⚠️ THE LOOP BELOW IS BYTE-IDENTICAL IN ALL FIVE BUILD-SPECS. If the list changes,
    # it changes in all five in the same commit: a family that differs by box is the
    # exact confusion this ruling removed.
    # ⚠️ AND IT STILL MAY NOT BE FOLDED INTO droste::blank_is_unset — that helper's
    # callers are audited against what each box's .cfg EXPOSES, and vllm's suite asserts
    # exactly that ("every guarded name is exposed by vllm.cfg"). A separate loop is how
    # the family stays identical on all five without making that check false on one.
    local _xdg
    for _xdg in XDG_DATA_HOME XDG_CONFIG_HOME XDG_STATE_HOME XDG_CACHE_HOME \
                XDG_RUNTIME_DIR XDG_DATA_DIRS XDG_CONFIG_DIRS; do
        if [ -n "${!_xdg+set}" ] && [ -z "${!_xdg}" ]; then
            unset "$_xdg"
        fi
    done

    # ComfyUI writes preview/scratch files under <base>/temp, which the SURFACES
    # row above binds from /opt/program-cache/tmp. Neither the baked dir nor a
    # freshly created src is user-writable in the distrobox lane, so make it
    # sticky world-writable (like /tmp) here — PRE_LAUNCH runs after the mounts,
    # so this lands on the mounted dir and both lanes can write to it whatever
    # uid they run as.
    mkdir -p /opt/ComfyUI/temp && chmod 1777 /opt/ComfyUI/temp
    # Absolute for the same reason the service head is — see the COMFYUI_ARGV_HEAD
    # comment. This one had NOT visibly failed (it ran through /usr/bin/python3 in
    # the distrobox lane and its imports happened to resolve), but "happened to" is
    # the whole problem: it is one system package away from silently classifying
    # against a different library set than the build pinned.
    /opt/venv/bin/python3 /opt/resources/scripts/model_scanner.py sync \
        || resolve::warn "model_scanner sync failed (exit $?) — model tree may be stale"
    # 🚨 PRE_LAUNCH RUNS AS ROOT FROM BOTH DOORS, so everything the scanner just wrote
    # belongs to the container's root — a host subuid under keep-id, i.e. NOT the user
    # the service then runs as. save_registry writes a temp file and RENAMES it over the
    # target (model_scanner.py: tmp.replace(path)), so the registry becomes root-owned on
    # every sync even when it was the user's a moment earlier, and the tree's category
    # dirs are root-owned from the run that first created them. Hand both back.
    # ⚠️ NOT run behind the privilege drop instead: PRE_LAUNCH ASSIGNS SERVICE in its
    # caller's shell (llama/ds4/vllm rebuild the whole argv there), so it can never be a
    # subprocess. And a user-run scanner could not replace an already-root-owned registry
    # on the boxes that have one — reclaiming works for those, privdropping would not.
    serve::_own /opt/data/model-registry.yaml
    serve::_own_dirs /opt/data/model-tree
    # LAST, and after CFG_FILE has been sourced: turn the user's comfyui.cfg into
    # the argv the server will actually run.
    comfyui_argv
    cd /opt/ComfyUI
}
